ure hits  everybody clears out of the way so sure  in theory in film theory it wouldn't be  all that hard for a rival studio to see  something like eternals or black widow  on the slate some of the riskier bets  for marvel and then release their movie  on the same weekend to steal away some  of marvel's thunder tap it at the knees  from there the rival studio would take  the number one slot for the weekend and  show the world that marvel isn't the  invincible force that it appears to be  suddenly the seal of marvel's vacuum  hold over the movie industry is broken  mickey gets an embarrassing black eye  and press and pr momentum carries it  from there i mean we've seen this done  before with other juggernauts it's  actually how the reality tv show  survivor managed to kill off who wants  to be a millionaire back when it was  king of prime time which in and of  itself is a really cool story hopefully  i can figure out a way to shove into one  of these someday i mean venom 2's  opening weekend of 90 million actually  would have passed three out of four  marvel projects this year it would have  beaten eternals black widow and shangshi  heck even f9 would have come close there  is vulnerability in these movies i just  don't think anyone actually wants to  take their shots why not what's everyone  so afraid of well i suspect the fear is  that marvel is so big that if they go  down way too much of the movie business  is brought down with them it's that too  big to fail problem all over again right  now people are excited to go see new  marvel movies on big screens that is  what's single-handedly keeping the  theater experience alive if marvel  suddenly goes away well theaters take  another big hit the media that covers  marvel takes a big hit movie culture as  a whole takes a huge step back and  nothing can truly fill the vacuum right  now at least nothing in hollywood can  fill that vacuum right now but youtube  can tick-tock can at the end of the day  going to see a movie is an expensive  inconvenience surveys report that 70 of  people would rather just stay at home to  watch a movie and that isn't just a  pandemic thing this was being reported  on back in 2014 and again in 2017 in the  middle of marvel mania while box office  earnings have been surging every year  the actual number of tickets sold has  been on a steady decline since 2002 as  fewer people are going to the movies  simply put it's an antiquated  entertainment format that as tvs have  gotten better and better has lost more  and more of its relevance marvel is the  one thing currently that can get people  to make going into the theater to watch  a movie a priority in their life and if  it suddenly goes away movies have lost  their last major foothold that time then  goes to cheaper more convenient  entertainment options video games  streaming social media digital video and  maybe they realize that there are  suddenly more fun things to do on a  friday night than sitting in a sticky  theater i mean in the last four years  alone the number of kids who watch  online video every day has more than  doubled it's not so much marvel vs other  movies it's the medium of movies versus  every other form of entertainment and in  that fight marvel is throwing far and  away the biggest hands so will the mcu  go away no because disney and the entire  movie industry will make sure that it  doesn't go away anytime soon but will  the invincibility of the mcu go away  yeah each year it's becoming more  vulnerable there's only so many times  that you can pull an end game or a no  way home you can't keep one-upping  yourself forever in fact scaling out  that big that quickly might have even  shot themselves in the foot everything  less than a three-way movie collab feels  missable feels like non-essential  viewing at this point so in summary what  can kill marvel well a few things as i  see it one over extension of the brand  and over emphasis of all the streaming  stuff i mean no one wants going to the  movies to feel like having to do  homework two kevin feige just piecing  out as the guy who's been driving this  whole ship towards one creative vision  after all we saw what happened with both  star wars and harry potter bad  leadership immediately destroys what  otherwise seems like a bulletproof brand  but the biggest thing that can truly  kill off the mcu is number three us it's  stuff like this video the analog horror  stuff that we cover here on youtube the  indie games that are happening over on  game theory stupid tick tocks that  everyone's trying to recreate insert  your favorite content creator here at  the end of the day the mcu's true  superpower is its cultural relevance the  fact that it's proven itself worthy of  your time but it's walking on a  tightrope one wrong step or heck not  even a few boring movies and the  relevance is lost the momentum is gone  you're off the train and do you hop back  on minecraft just had a big update and  oh man mr beast just recreated squid  game whoa mandela catalog just updated  and what was i talking about again oh  yeah the mcu stuff yeah i guess i'll get  around to watching hawkeye at some point  what is it they say this is the way the  marvel cinematic universe ends not with  a bang but with a whimper but hey that's  just a theory a film theory and cut  [Music]  [Music]  foreign
 

